feat(memory): persist conversation across launches via ConversationStore

Completed the memory foundation: ConversationStore (SQLite) is now the
single persisted source of truth behind the in-memory conversation
window, so cross-turn memory survives app relaunch.

- ConversationManager: restore-on-start (loadPersistedHistory, bounded
  newest window, idempotent, duplicate-write guard), recordInteraction
  writes user+assistant pairs through to the store exactly once; a
  refusal records only the user request - a failed action can never
  become a fabricated successful turn in memory.
- ConversationStore.loadMessages now returns the NEWEST N messages in
  chronological order (rowid ordering; a naive ASC LIMIT returned the
  oldest turns); added messageCount for bounded-window diagnostics.
- AgentLoop records every route through the same recordInteraction path
  (one source of truth, no second copy); DirectComposer falls back to
  the persisted window when the in-memory one is empty (fresh
  lifecycle).
- AppDelegate and the --goals CLI mode restore the persisted window at
  lifecycle start; CLI paths allow the detached persist write to land
  before exit.
- Focused regressions: exact-once persistence + ordering, restore after
  lifecycle reset + idempotence, bounded newest-window clipping,
  no-fabricated-success on failure, and memory-never-authorizes
  (PermissionGate denial unchanged with memory present).

Authority untouched: memory is context only - PermissionGate,
PlanValidator, CommandSandbox, ReferenceResolver, and TaskStateMachine
are unchanged, and emergency stop remains independent of memory.

